+  Key design decisions:
+  - OT model: single authoritative transform point. Each op carries a base version; stale ops (version < current) are transformed against every intervening applied op from the in-session history, guaranteeing
+  convergence. Ops without a version apply at HEAD.
+  - Same-position insert tie-break: position >= insertPos shifts right, so concurrent inserts at the same spot both survive deterministically.
+  - Concurrency safety: message handlers are fully synchronous (better-sqlite3 is sync), so per-document ops never interleave.
+  - Persistence: default rollback journal commits straight to the main DB file; active_connections cleared on every createDatabase so a restart always reports 0 live connections.
